sycl: one pass over the scores and batched KV heads in the MKL flash-attention path

HomeBrain patch on ggml-sycl. Applies on top of 0015.
Upstream tracking: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/32757

The online softmax computed every score twice, for the row maximum and for
the numerators; with an indexed bias that is two gathers per score. Pass 1
now stores the final score in place and pass 2 reads it. The work-groups of
one query in different heads run next to each other, so they share the mask,
bias index and bias table lines in cache. Q packing and normalization are one
launch per pass instead of one per Q head, and when one chunk of the scores of
all KV heads fits 24M elements (the sliding-window layers of a prefill), the
KV heads run in one pass with batched GEMMs (GGML_SYCL_MKL_FA_BATCH_HEADS=0
turns that off). Inkling's attention at a 512-token ubatch, q8_0 K/V, GQA 3
on the Arc Pro B60: 5.60 -> 1.53 ms at 1536 keys (its sliding-window layers),
7.96 -> 4.21 ms at 4096, 12.17 -> 8.66 ms at 10240 and 20.3 -> 15.8 ms at
20480.

